# Technical glossary: exact concepts and examples, avoid jargon-only entries
terms=[
('Alpha channel','An extra channel storing transparency, often 0 transparent to 1 opaque.','A lower third with transparent background needs an alpha-capable format.',53),('Aspect ratio','Displayed width divided by height.','1920/1080 = 16:9; 1080/1920 = 9:16.',3),('Bit depth','Number of signal levels per channel before processing/encoding.','8-bit has 256 code values per channel; 10-bit has 1024.',56),('Bitrate','Data per second of encoded stream.','8 Mb/s for 10 s is about 10 MB before overhead.',84),('B-roll','Supporting picture over the primary story.','Show the product while narration explains its mechanism.',34),('CBR','Constant bitrate aims for predictable stream size.','A broadcaster may specify CBR.',86),('Chroma subsampling','Reduced color resolution relative to brightness.','4:2:0 sacrifices chroma detail versus 4:2:2.',13),('Clip instance','A placement of referenced media in a sequence.','Same camera file used twice at different in/out ranges.',1),('Codec','Compression/decompression method for a stream.','H.264 or ProRes is not a folder or container.',84),('Container','File wrapper that houses encoded streams and metadata.','MP4 may contain H.264 video and AAC audio.',84),('Crossfade','Overlapping audio levels that smooth transitions.','Two room-tone clips crossfade over 8 frames.',43),('dBFS','Decibels relative to digital full scale.','0 dBFS is the upper digital sample peak limit.',38),('Drop-frame timecode','Labeling adjustment at 29.97-related cadence; actual video frames are not discarded.','Some timecode frame numbers are skipped to align clock labels.',2),('Dynamic Link','Adobe inter-application linking between timelines/compositions.','Linked After Effects composition appears in Premiere.',95),('Frame rate','Frames displayed per second (nominal or exact).','25 fps frames have 40 ms intervals.',2),('Gamma','Nonlinear relationship between code values and light/display intensity.','Incorrect gamma interpretation changes midtone appearance.',61),('GOP','Group of Pictures; compression referencing frames over time.','Long-GOP camera codec can be hard to scrub.',84),('Headroom','Level margin before clipping or target maximum.','Dialogue peaks below 0 dBFS leave room for transient summation.',45),('HEVC','High Efficiency Video Coding / H.265.','Usually more efficient compression than H.264 but variable decode support.',85),('HDR','High dynamic range encoding and display path.','PQ/HLG footage needs managed transforms for SDR exports.',56),('In point','First chosen frame in a marked range.','Source In at frame 50 and Out near 100 selects a portion.',16),('Interframe','Compression that predicts frames from other frames.','Long-GOP codecs use interframe prediction.',85),('Intraframe','Compression of each frame substantially independently.','ProRes is commonly chosen for edit intermediates.',85),('J-cut','Incoming audio begins before its matching video.','Hear the next speaker before seeing them.',27),('Keyframe','Time/value control point for animated property.','Scale goes 100% to 110% in 2 seconds.',48),('L-cut','Outgoing audio continues under the next picture.','Keep interviewer speaking beneath illustrative B-roll.',27),('Log','Camera encoding that preserves wide scene range with low contrast preview.','Normalize camera Log before creative grading.',56),('Loudness (LUFS)','Perceptual program loudness measurement.','Integrated LUFS describes the complete segment.',45),('LUT','Lookup table mapping input to output values.','Technical Log transform and creative LUT serve distinct roles.',60),('Master','High-quality intended deliverable or source reference.','Retain source camera masters and edit-friendly output master.',88),('Metadata','Descriptors about footage and edits.','Timecode, duration, reel, frame rate and tags.',11),('Mono','One channel of audio signal.','Lavalier dialogue is often mono.',40),('Motion estimation','An algorithm predicting movement between images.','Optical Flow may warp a fast-moving hand.',29),('Multicam','Multiple synchronized cameras in one editorial source.','Cut between two synced interview angles.',69),('Nonlinear editing','Editing through references rather than irreversible linear recording.','Move a clip anywhere without cutting the camera file.',1),('Out point','Boundary defining the end of a chosen source/sequence range.','Mark after the sentence, then insert only the selection.',16),('Paper Edit','Transcript-based selection and rough-sequence creation in 26.5.','Select two statements to generate a new sequence.',66),('Peak','Maximum instantaneous signal amplitude.','A loud clap peaks higher than sustained dialogue.',38),('Pixel aspect ratio','Shape of individual sample pixels.','Modern HD often uses square pixels; legacy media may not.',3),('Playhead','Position of current playback/edit time.','Move playhead to 00:00:10:00 before adding marker.',19),('Premiere project','Editable set of media pointers, bins and sequences.','A .prproj alone does not contain camera originals.',8),('Preview render','Temporary media rendered to improve playback.','Green render bar does not prove final export quality.',83),('Proxy','Alternate lower-cost file attached to master.','Edit 4K originals with 720p proxies.',14),('Rec.709','SDR video color primaries/transfer conventions.','Common SDR broadcast/web delivery target.',56),('Ripple edit','Boundary trim moving later sequence content.','Shorten A by 10 frames; B begins 10 frames earlier.',22),('Rolling edit','Boundary trim that transfers duration across adjacent clips.','Grow A 10 frames and shrink B 10 frames; no length change.',23),('Sequence','Timeline and settings defining an edit.','1080p25 sequence stores tracks and timebase.',15),('Slip edit','Shift source content while keeping clip sequence interval fixed.','Use earlier part of reaction shot without moving the cut.',24),('Slide edit','Move a clip in sequence by trimming neighbors.','Shift middle insert without changing its own source range.',25),('Source patching','Choose destination tracks for inserted source audio/video.','Patch V source to V2 before inserting an overlay.',18),('Sync Lock','Track rule about participation in ripple edits.','Lock allows protected alignment decisions.',26),('Timecode','Frame-address display in hours:minutes:seconds:frames.','00:01:10:12 is a position, not 70.12 seconds.',2),('Track targeting','Sequence-track designation for many timeline operations.','Track-target highlight differs from source V1 patch.',18),('True peak','Estimated peaks between reconstructed digital samples.','Output limiter may target true-peak ceiling.',45),('Variable frame rate','Nonconstant video capture frame intervals.','Phone footage may require CFR transcoding for sync.',13),('VBR','Variable bitrate reallocates data with picture complexity.','Action may use more bits than a static slate.',86),('White balance','Relative channel correction for neutral reference.','Correct warm orange camera cast before look.',57),('Working color space','Internal processing representation for tone/color.','May differ from source and output color space.',56),('XML interchange','Structured data for supported editorial exchange.','Not every effect/transcript transfers between editors.',75)]
glossary=[{'term':t,'definition':d,'example':e,'lesson':f'L{n:03}'} for t,d,e,n in terms]
